>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_unsafe_solver`

``` hol4
simpLib.add_unsafe_solver : Traverse.ssolver -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a named unsafe solver to a simpset.

A solver has type

``` hol4
type ssolver = {name : string, solve : simp_prover_ctxt -> term -> thm}
type simp_prover_ctxt =
  {stack : term list, context_thms : thm list, recurse : term -> thm}
```

`solve ctxt c` must prove `c` or raise `HOL_ERR`. In `ctxt`, `stack`
holds the side conditions being proved, `context_thms` the theorems in
scope (supplied theorems, assumptions and congruence-rule context), and
`recurse c` simplifies `c`, returning `|- c = c'`.

Unsafe solvers prove side conditions of conditional rewrites: once the
subgoaler has reduced a condition `c` to `c'` other than `T`, the unsafe
solvers are tried on `c'` in order. They are also the final solvers of
`GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false}`, and hence of `SIMP_TAC` and its
relatives.

`add_unsafe_solver solver ss` appends `solver` unless `ss` already has
an unsafe solver of the same name. `Excl name` in a theorem list
disables the solver for that call.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val decide = {name = "decide", solve = K DECIDE} : Traverse.ssolver;
>>+ SIMP_CONV bool_ss [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD] “x MOD (x + 1)”;
>> SIMP_CONV (simpLib.add_unsafe_solver decide bool_ss)
     [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD] “x MOD (x + 1)”;
```

